    Unscrupulous sellers often engage in "batch-swapping"—advertising a listing as high-tier GX or LJR, but shipping a cheap VT or budget batch to the agent warehouse, pocketing the price difference. 
  </p>
  <p>
    This is why relying on an actively maintained, community-reviewed catalog like the <strong><a href="/">Kakobuy Spreadsheet</a></strong> is indispensable. Curators constantly monitor seller return rates and warehouse QC photos to blackball bait-and-switch merchants, ensuring that when you pay for a premium batch, you actually receive the real deal.
